# ── python targets: DERIVED FROM THE STAGE3 SEED, not frozen here ────────────
# This file is a placeholder. The builder OVERWRITES it in the sysroot with the
# seed-derived, ADDITIVE delta line
#     */* PYTHON_TARGETS: <targets the seed's own installed packages carry>
# via scripts/_python-targets-lib.sh (pt_apply_seed_targets), at the same moment
# it appends the matching PYTHON_TARGETS/PYTHON_SINGLE_TARGET to make.conf.
#
# WHY NO LITERAL LIVES HERE ANY MORE — two real fleet failures, mirror images of
# each other, both caused by a frozen python3_NN (see docs/PYTHON-TARGETS-SEED-DRIFT.md):
#
#   * 2026-07-16, jetson edge_ai (session 20260715-235432). The seed was built
#     for 3.12 while the tree's profile default had moved past it, so freshly
#     pulled ebuilds (setuptools-83 / setuptools-scm-10.2 -> jaraco-text,
#     hatchling, flit-core, urllib3, jinja2, cython, ...) came up with
#     python_targets_python3_12 UNSET and the payload emerge aborted behind
#         "The following USE changes are necessary to proceed:
#          >=dev-python/...  python_targets_python3_12"
#     The literal "python3_12" seeded here fixed that — for that seed.
#
#   * 2026-07-29, the 11-image mesh build (session 20260729-233913-719d4e). The
#     amd64 seed had moved to 3.13+3.14 with NO 3.12, so the SAME literal now
#     pointed at an interpreter the seed did not have: the seed's installed
#     portage/gemato kept demanding python_targets_python3_13/14 from
#     dev-python/{requests,certifi,charset-normalizer,idna,urllib3,pysocks}
#     while our config forced those slots to 3_12 only ->
#         "!!! Multiple package instances within a single package slot ...
#          resulting in a slot conflict"
#     -> resolution aborted -> "stage4 payload incomplete".
#
# The invariant that survives both, and every future stage3 python bump:
# PYTHON_TARGETS must be a SUPERSET of what the SEED's own installed packages
# were built with. That is a build-time fact, so it is computed at build time.
#
# FORMAT NOTE (man 5 portage): a package.use USE_EXPAND line is a DELTA that ADDS
# to the profile default — "if you need to remove earlier assignments or
# defaults, you need to explicitly specify '-*'". Never write '-*' here; that
# turns the widening back into the replacement that caused the outage.
# PYTHON_SINGLE_TARGET is never set in a '*/*' line: it is ^^ exactly-one in
# REQUIRED_USE, and a wildcard delta can enable two.
